From 6d4adee41b5ce7508cb332f9ece05cf218adcb2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compartments: stop what changed, retry failed mirrors, keep
 Automatic places

Fixes from the review of the policy service (ADR-208):

- A change of profile, sensor value, location value or place stops the packages concerned two seconds later (after the readers of the files looked again): a process read its time zone, country and operator once, a GNSS listener or a direct sensor channel keeps what it was given. Defaults changes stop nothing (known limit).
- A failed mirror write is tried again on the background thread, after 10 s, doubling to 5 minutes, until all mirrors are written.
- An Automatic app keeps the place of the last persona table when it was Automatic and substituted before, so a boot without a network neither moves the persona nor revokes the location permissions.
- The persona and sensor files get their mode (0644) on the temporary file before the rename, never 0600 under the final name.
- The package removal receiver cannot throw, and ignores a removal for one user while the package is installed for another.
- ACCESS_MEDIA_LOCATION is taken with the other location permissions; CellSubset no longer formats the mnc with the default locale.
